This container image (semiont-smelter) includes the following third-party
components:

  Alpine Linux - MIT License
  Python - Python Software Foundation License
  tini - MIT License

  tesseract-ocr (Tesseract, the OCR engine: the `tesseract` program) - Apache-2.0 License
    https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract
    Installed as Alpine Linux packages it. Alpine installs with it the
    packages it depends on, each as Alpine built it. The image's own record
    names every one of them (`apk info`), and the license Alpine states for
    each (`apk info --license <name>`). Semiont links none of them: the
    Smelter runs `tesseract` as a program of its own. The source of each,
    and of Tesseract as packaged, is Alpine's
    (https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports), at the release of Alpine
    the image is built on, which /etc/alpine-release in the image names.
  tesseract-ocr-data-eng (the English language data Tesseract reads with) - Apache-2.0 License
    Installed as Alpine Linux packages it.

  Python packages built into the image from this repository:
    semiont - Apache-2.0 License (The AI Alliance)
    semiont-service - Apache-2.0 License (The AI Alliance)
    semiont-smelter - Apache-2.0 License (The AI Alliance)
    semiont-vectors - Apache-2.0 License (The AI Alliance)

  Python packages installed at build time from https://pypi.org, each at the
  version apps/smelter/uv.lock pins: what those four require. Among them:
    pypdfium2 - BSD-3-Clause OR Apache-2.0 License
      The binding the Smelter reads a PDF through. Its wheel carries PDFium
      itself, Chromium's PDF library (BSD-3-Clause OR Apache-2.0), and the
      libraries built into it, each under its own license.

Each package from pypi.org carries its license text in its
<name>-<version>.dist-info directory within the image, under the
site-packages directory of /opt/venv. The wheel of pypdfium2 carries the
license texts of PDFium and of what is built into it as well. The four built
from this repository are under the license beside this file.
